10-
11:Follow the required schema and lifecycle in [CHANGELOG.md](../CHANGELOG.md). At scope inspection, search existing IDs; create a record for a new defect/change before implementation, with actual versus expected and source. At implementation, record the cause, mapping/specification → code chain and affected files; use `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED` until checks finish. Record each material failure and reopening immediately under the same ID. At verification, append actual commands/screenshots/results, date, verifier and the applicable auditor verdict. Only evidence-backed technical approval permits `VERIFIED`. Explicit user approval is recorded independently and is never inferred from silence. At delivery, reconcile the current status/index and link remaining open defects. Do this autonomously for small fixes as well as large tasks; use a compact record when appropriate.
12-
13-Root-cause analysis must identify the agent decision/action, technical mechanism, missed control, evidence-backed responsibility and the behavior to change. Use the CHANGELOG classifications; missing or additional input is not automatically user fault. Unknown historical details stay unknown. Before similar work or rebuilding, load relevant causes/lessons and convert prevention into checks. Link repeatable errors to [Agent Eval](agent-evals.md); update case results only after actual runs, independently of fix approval.
14-
