ed network barrier before claiming cached switches, and test pending/failed cold requests separately; a short local timeout cannot prove a public runtime defect. For iOS fullscreen-viewer corrections, inspect rendered wrapper ancestry, verify solid document backing when modal/backdrop paint is suppressed, hide explicit-visibility descendants, restore landing colors/scroll/focus, and inspect changing portrait heights and short landscape control/frame overlap. Never count emulated content screenshots as native Safari/Telegram chrome evidence. For a founder loading/fullscreen correction, specify four HeatCore and two CyberMind originals: first two per group asynchronously after window load, remaining two only on opening, retain successful transfer/decoded DOM image. Hold initial bytes at25% and actual DOM decode; no photo or copy before readiness, true percent only with reliable length and indeterminate otherwise. White only inside full-width nine-slice metal contour; proportional photo/title keeps one source ratio through changing heights. If the customer rejects inner side bands, reopen the geometry defect: full-width contour does not prove full-width photo. Quantify source/window aspect mismatch, check six source-aligned label/diagram regions, and disclose that unchanged fixed artwork cannot simultaneously fill both axes, retain all pixels and avoid scrolling at unequal ratios. Analysis-first scope must not silently implement a changed gesture policy; propose width-fit/internal pan versus responsive per-slide recomposition with independent photo-width, ratio, full-content and pending-scroll checks. After width-priority implementation, use native vertical pan/keyboard for content and group buttons for group changes; verify momentum/pending/error freeze, committed top reset, actual touch/RTL, all six slides/locales and the final integrated keyboard focus test. Update every old IMG/src consumer when moving to nine-slice/blob retained images and wait for actual visible-media/decode barriers; a selected suite that omits stale tests cannot certify all consumer integration. Stop at horizontal endpoints and reverse; lock required input, cancel in-flight smooth scroll and retain focus/Close/Retry. Exercise real corrupt HTTP200 cache without routing, explicit Retry despite automatic browser attempts, native replacement-load/decode order, no-JS and HTTP200 script throw/rejection before hydration. Inspect effective loading contrast including reduced-motion opacity; old scroll/wheel/CTA tests must wait for actual readiness before ordinary input, while separate pending tests verify locks. Serialize framework build before generated-type checks. Verify each changed journal ID contains its own dated technical approval and matching index lifecycle; bound insertion at the earliest next ID anchor or heading, never leave prior-ID verdicts below the next ID anchor. A neighboring entry or index alone is insufficient. For the vertical-white-band follow-up, independently measure all four photo/cutout edges and zero internal scroll when the proportional full-width source fits. Bound frame height to the photo plus source-scaled metal borders; never stretch or crop to remove surplus white space. Inspect393×852, Pro/Max and short-window top/bottom captures. Post-hydration viewer tests await hydration and media readiness; preserve parallel timeout failures and rerun without concurrent browser load before approval. For CHG0073 instruction validation, use the existing artwork-color-pipeline geometry mode even for CSS-only photo adaptation; keep separate photo/frame width, proportional height and content access checks, without re-encoding unchanged originals. Consolidate diagnosis and verification into the existing viewer topic, retain raw evidence and historical verdicts, and repair relocated links. For the retained-main follow-up, inject a delayed far landing tile and held/corrupt optional gallery prefetch. Reject covering ready content, blocking upward input, or entering unfinished pixels. Require a native downward frontier, unchanged ready viewport pixels, all-main high-priority background requests after hero actual decode, all-six low-priority gallery warm independent of the landing guard, and real wheel/touch/FAQ/resize checks. For an explicitly requested two-ribbon stage, supersede prior contour/slide policies: four HeatCore plus two CyberMind full-width proportional planes, one semantic title per group, no numbered callouts or bottom controls, two top group dots, literal rightward next/leftward previous even in Arabic. Preserve callout label x/width after removing numeric prefixes; inspect every source-local body and all four empty-edge blended joins on both phones. Preserve six original asynchronous low-priority post-load transfers and retained decoded elements; commit complete groups atomically with aggregate reliable bytes/indeterminate fallback and old-group retention. Test complete Tab/ShiftTab cycles including region and pending state, bounded native wheel events, actual touch/RTL and all locales/widths. Stable captures need real image/font readiness plus paint settlement; never call a timing barrier a runtime fix. Reproduce unexplained retained-artwork loss on an untouched host baseline, preserve failed evidence, keep unrelated defects open, and preserve historical approved PNG bytes when rerunning old suites. Before committing new untracked evidence, verify the exact staged scope and staged whitespace; preserve raw log originals during whitespace-only normalization and never alter outcomes. Controlled agent run: `NOT_RUN`; current browser regression passes do not constitute this controlled agent run. |
