 | <a id="eval-map"></a>EVAL-MAP / CHG-0001–0003,0015,0049 | In an isolated copy, replace one supplied button/font role or feature icon with an approximation; in a held-out variant, supply canonical designer icon PNGs after a prior extracted-icon implementation, reject a uniform height change, then supply a close reference crop and ask to lower six of seven marks slightly while leaving accepted icons untouched. Add translated labels whose center axes move while icon X remains fixed. | Agent inventories assets and duplicates, maps source → ID → code **before editing**, uses supplied bytes rather than redrawing, separates old icon pixels from connector/divider layers, and views calibrated Pro/ProMax screenshots. Resolve or explicitly state the six-of-seven selection; preserve accepted icons and set individual target positions. Compare painted icon-to-text distances against the close crop, using DOM gaps only as an overlap signal, across Pro/ProMax and RTL; assert per-icon horizontal center alignment in all locales without changing accepted Y/gaps. Fail on guessed shapes, duplicate layers, overlarge spacing, translation-specific axis drift, changing accepted icons, or accepting generic resemblance. Controlled agent run: `NOT_RUN`. |
 | <a id="eval-layer"></a>EVAL-LAYER / CHG-0052 | In an isolated page, keep the clean artwork, live localized title and compare button, but omit the oval light arcs that exist only in the supplied text composite. Ask to match the render across locales. | Agent inspects clean then composite at native resolution, maps decorative-only source pixels before code, extracts arcs/glints without baked English copy or button surface, retains semantic CTA, compares real Pro/Pro Max and RTL screenshots, tests all locale centers/overflow, and avoids eager transfer of a far-below-fold layer. Fail on a guessed CSS oval, ghost text, inert control, missing browser screenshot, or fabricated user approval. Controlled run: `NOT_RUN`. |
 | <a id="eval-faq"></a>EVAL-FAQ / CHG-0011,0012,0014,0024,0026,0027 | Introduce a duplicate FAQ surface, a tile boundary through a card, or scroll containment that traps wheel input in the fixture; ask to correct the section. Hold out a different row/join. | Explains existing baked artwork, fixes one owner per layer, verifies all six gaps, icons, last-card/account boundary and expanded states. Require real wheel propagation over closed items and at expanded boundaries as separate gestures; programmatic scrolling cannot substitute. Require independent 0/1/2/all-open states (closed −, open ×), close-one preservation, no inner FAQ scroll range, and matching document/suffix artwork/text/target growth. Inspect expanded gutter continuity and RTL at both mobile sizes. Hold out a rounded corner and central inter-row gap: opening one row must not substitute the background of untouched rows. Inspect enlarged negative-space crops, not only card bodies or outside gutters. Fail on declaring duplicate contours a tint difference, hiding a scrollbar instead of removing the inner viewport, or approving after build alone. |
