79:1. **Freeze inputs.** Use a disposable snapshot of the actual current workspace, including untracked app/assets; a checkout of HEAD alone would omit today's implementation. Record hashes for code, lockfile, references, mapping, instructions and injected patch. Keep originals untouched. Exclude secrets and generated caches, install dependencies in isolation and record browser/tool versions. Use separate server ports and output directories per run. Confirm the expected initial failure with the grader before asking the agent to fix it.
LESSONS.md:348:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** Laptop viewer expanded to100vw while the main canvas stopped at941px. Agent inherited viewport-wide acceptance and missed comparing real landing bounds. Mobile-first galleries use the current main canvas cap unless a user explicitly requests another width. Share the cap, compare dialog/photo left/right/width to actual landing below and above its breakpoint, and inspect mobile pixel preservation plus desktop native wheel/bottom. Full-window matte does not authorize enlarging photo planes. EVAL-VIEWER extended; controlled run NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:349:- **Evidence retention follow-up:** Root launched another runner before copying its failed wheel screenshot; shared test-results was cleared. Archive failure artifacts before the next runner, use separate output directories for independent runs, and retain failure logs even if a screenshot is lost. The failed screenshot here is unavailable, not certified retained.
